pumac-2014-combinatorics-b-01.body:
Measure time in minutes after 8:00. The girl arrives at $g\in[0,60]$, the guy at $u\in[-60,30]$, uniformly and independently, so the sample space is a $60\times90$ rectangle of area $5400$. They fall in love when $|g-u|\le10$. For each $u$ the favourable length of $g$ is:

- $-10\le u\le0$: $g\in[0,u+10]$, length $u+10$; total area $\int_{-10}^0(u+10)\,du=50$;
- $0\le u\le10$: $g\in[0,u+10]$, length $u+10$; area $\int_0^{10}(u+10)\,du=150$;
- $10\le u\le30$: $g\in[u-10,u+10]\subset[0,60]$, length $20$; area $400$.

(For $u<-10$ they never meet.) Favourable area $=50+150+400=600$, so the probability is $\frac{600}{5400}=\frac19$ and $p+q=10$.

**Answer: 10**
